@format 1
@id functionality.media-loading.common.backend
@title Media loading — common backend load
@section Functionality
@area Media loading — Common
@entry backend-start
@summary Trace LMediaLoadAsync through path validation, request ownership, ffprobe, generation checks, and backend outcomes.
@related functionality.media-loading.common.completion
@tag media
@tag loading
@tag common
@tag ffprobe

@alias media-load = Cadroue.Media.LMediaLoad
@alias media = Cadroue.Media.LMedia
@alias custody = Cadroue.Core.LCustody

[backend-start] Backend load dispatch <input>
- Start the asynchronous backend media-load operation for the requested source @ media-load.LMediaLoadAsync(...)
> path-check

[path-check] Backend path normalization <decision>
- Normalize the requested source to a full path and reject invalid path syntax immediately @ media-load.LMediaLoadAsync(...)
  @ media-load.LMediaLoadReject(...)
? "Path normalized" > request-owner
? "Invalid path syntax" > path-failure

[path-failure] Path-normalization failure <error>
- Create and raise the immediate rejected load outcome @ media-load.LMediaLoadReject(...)
> map:functionality.media-loading.common.completion

[request-owner] Backend request ownership <process>
- Cancel and dispose the previous request, create a linked cancellation source, advance the generation, and mark the new request pending @ media-load.LMediaLoadAsync(...)
> source-check

[source-check] Backend source validation <decision>
- Require a nonblank path, an existing file, and a supported media extension @ media-load.LMediaLoadAsync(...)
  @ media.LMediaCheck(...)
? "Supported existing media" > ffprobe-read
? "Missing, blank, or unsupported" > source-failure

[source-failure] Source-validation failure <error>
- Clear pending state and create the current failure outcome @ media-load.LMediaLoadFailCurrent(...)
> map:functionality.media-loading.common.completion

[ffprobe-read] FFprobe media inspection <external>
- Run the media reader off the caller thread, launch ffprobe for stream and format JSON, attach the process to custody, and kill its process tree on cancellation @ media-load.LMediaLoadAsync(...)
  @ media.LMediaFfprobeRead(...)
  @ custody.LCustodyAttach(...)
> ffprobe-result

[ffprobe-result] FFprobe result interpretation <process>
- Reject nonzero exit, empty output, or invalid JSON and otherwise parse duration and first video/audio stream information @ media.LMediaFfprobeRead(...)
  @ media.LMediaFfprobeParse(...)
> generation-check

[generation-check] Backend generation check <decision>
- Suppress results after disposal or supersession and classify current failure/cancellation versus current parsed media @ media-load.LMediaLoadAsync(...)
  @ media-load.LMediaLoadFailCurrent(...)
? "Superseded or disposed" > obsolete
? "Current load failed or cancelled" > current-failure
? "Current media information" > success-commit

[obsolete] Obsolete backend result <output>
= The request returns Obsolete without raising LMediaLoadCompleted.

[current-failure] Current backend failure <error>
- Clear pending state and create the current failure or cancellation outcome @ media-load.LMediaLoadFailCurrent(...)
> map:functionality.media-loading.common.completion

[success-commit] Backend media commit <storage>
- Clear pending state, store the current media path and parsed media information, and create the successful load outcome @ media-load.LMediaLoadAsync(...)
> map:functionality.media-loading.common.completion
